From 292d147233aca8f92f8641a68f11887566598b21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TripleU <182648541+TripleU613@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:28:25 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] kboot: T6050: drive the full panel, notch rows included, by
 default

Unless m1n1.conf says chosen.asahi,show-notch=0, set it on T6050 before the DT
is built, so the boot framebuffer keeps iBoot's full height and appledrm uses
the firmware-27 DCP's full timing instead of trimming the notch rows. As
edimoldovan's J714c kernel does (linux-aurora 4d11ac10a012, "show the notch
rows by default", 3024x1964 through the DCP on his J714c). On TripleU613's
J714s with this and 0006's display default (no m1n1.conf lines): eDP-2
3024x1964@120, Hyprland on the full panel.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01H3rUWsmTuAiei3A7JojjHG
---
 src/kboot.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/kboot.c b/src/kboot.c
index b4c8ff3..58530d2 100644
--- a/src/kboot.c
+++ b/src/kboot.c
@@ -6885,6 +6885,17 @@ int kboot_prepare_dt(void *fdt)
         dt = NULL;
     }
 
+    /*
+     * T6050 MacBook Pros: drive the full panel, notch rows included, unless m1n1.conf says
+     * chosen.asahi,show-notch=0. The firmware-27 DCP already reports the full 3024x1964 timing;
+     * appledrm only trims it to the notch-less height when /chosen/asahi,show-notch is not 1, and
+     * this keeps the boot framebuffer at the same height. As edimoldovan's J714c kernel does
+     * (linux-aurora 4d11ac10a012, "show the notch rows by default"); omarchy-mac's
+     * display-cutouts.json keeps the bar clear of the notch.
+     */
+    if (chip_id == T6050 && !kboot_get_chosen("asahi,show-notch"))
+        kboot_set_chosen("asahi,show-notch", "1");
+
     /* Need to init ISP early to carve out heap */
     isp_init();
 
